{"status":"dry","notes":"The AusTender OCDS API is reachable with no login and returns OCDS 1.1 JSON, but I couldn't mine it with the tools I had. A one-month window (Jan 2025) returned about 186K characters. WebFetch only reads the first ~100K per call, and I had no Bash or PowerShell to download the file and filter it locally. The date filter also looks loose: the Jan 2025 window held releases dated 2025-06 to 2026-07 and dateSigned values from 2024. I read about 47 releases and found no Illumina, Element, MGI, Complete Genomics or Ultima supplier. That is a tiny sample of the 2019-2026 universe, so it says nothing about absence. A web search found no federal Illumina notice. The only aggregator hit, qld2032.com, lists 79 dated Illumina Aust awards, all to The University of Queensland (Nov 2021-Feb 2023, $11K-$168K each). That is the Queensland register already covered by S325, not federal data. Kit and assay awards in that list are small, with a $155K top in Aug 2022. No federal agency, procurement-method or limited-tender reason was captured. Federal Illumina purchases would probably be small (mostly under AUD 100K), and many would sit under panels or via distributors, so the yield is likely thin even if mined fully.","how_to_mine":"Needs a script, not WebFetch. For each month 2019-2026, curl https://api.tenders.gov.au/ocds/findByDates/contractPublished/{start}/{end} with short windows, then parse releases[].parties[].name for Illumina, Element, MGI, Complete Genomics and Ultima. Output agency (procuringEntity), contracts[].value.amount, dateSigned, description and tender.procurementMethod / procurementMethodRationale. Windows are fuzzy, so de-duplicate by ocid. Also try the human AusTender supplier search with the Illumina ABN. Separately, try tenders.gov.au CN-ID pages for CSIRO, ANSTO and NMI.","difficulty":"hard","items":[],"new_candidates":["Local scripted pull of the AusTender OCDS API (curl plus python -I), filtered by supplier name","Aggregator pages lik